00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:35.770
You need a hand, don't you?

00:01:37.680 --> 00:01:42.360
Ronja, who had almost met her end in the winter forest,

00:01:42.360 --> 00:01:46.860
was saved by Birk, and made a promise with him to become siblings.

00:01:47.780 --> 00:01:54.990
The next morning, Ronja couldn't bring herself to wake up and start her day as usual.

00:01:56.410 --> 00:02:00.960
Ronja was ill for the first time in her life.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:08.170
A Thing Done in Secret

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:08.170
A Thing Done in Secret

00:02:37.180 --> 00:02:39.450
What's the matter with you?

00:02:43.750 --> 00:02:45.130
What are you saying?

00:02:45.130 --> 00:02:47.250
You're not really ill, are you?

00:02:49.590 --> 00:02:52.430
Her fever's really high! She's burning up!

00:03:09.940 --> 00:03:12.030
I knew it at once.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:16.810
I knew this was going to happen.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:21.070
My daughter is going to be taken from me.

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:25.910
My daughter... My daughter...

00:03:25.910 --> 00:03:27.880
is going to die!

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:36.920
Oh dear...

00:03:43.660 --> 00:03:45.060
Hey, boss!

00:03:49.480 --> 00:03:51.110
Stop it, boss!

00:03:51.110 --> 00:03:53.400
Let go of me!

00:03:53.820 --> 00:03:57.370
If you keep this up, you'll terrify poor Ronja!

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:15.640
It's a good thing to rest and keep warm, my Ronja.

00:04:16.300 --> 00:04:18.890
That's what you have to do when you're ill.

00:04:20.890 --> 00:04:24.520
Don't be silly, Father.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.690
This is nothing.

00:04:29.690 --> 00:04:36.950
Because... it could have been much worse.

00:04:39.660 --> 00:04:41.080
Ronja!

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.510
<i>My Ronja... My dove...</i>

00:04:54.510 --> 00:04:58.260
<i>She's mourning because she doesn't want to die young, right?</i>

00:05:02.810 --> 00:05:05.180
Don't cry, little one...

00:05:06.270 --> 00:05:08.270
You'll soon be well again.

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.770
You will, for sure!

00:05:15.780 --> 00:05:18.070
It's just like a wake.

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.370
Lovis!

00:05:25.140 --> 00:05:26.920
Lovis!

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:36.340
Lovis!

00:05:54.070 --> 00:05:57.610
At this very moment our daughter's life is hanging on by a hair.

00:05:57.610 --> 00:05:59.240
What the hell is she doing?

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:03.410
It's a mother's duty to be by her child's side, isn't it?

00:06:21.970 --> 00:06:25.140
Why are you not with our sick child?!

00:06:25.550 --> 00:06:28.100
Do I have a sick child?

00:06:28.100 --> 00:06:29.700
I didn't know.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:33.640
I'll go as soon as I've fed the sheep.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.820
I can do that!

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:38.230
Go to Ronja!

00:06:38.950 --> 00:06:43.110
That is, if she's still alive...

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:54.170
Ronja, at least until you see your mother's face...

00:06:54.170 --> 00:06:56.200
don't die.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:32.620
Thus, Ronja spent three days in the bed.

00:07:34.250 --> 00:07:37.460
She had done a lot of thinking during that time

00:07:37.460 --> 00:07:41.800
and perhaps became a little more thoughtful than before.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:57.610
Birk, my brother...

00:07:57.610 --> 00:07:58.770
Ronja!

00:08:00.190 --> 00:08:04.150
My dove... here's your porridge.

00:08:07.490 --> 00:08:10.660
I've never lied to my father.

00:08:10.660 --> 00:08:16.670
But I could never tell him that I have a Borka for a sibling.

00:08:17.880 --> 00:08:25.800
Doing so would be like hitting him over the head with a sledgehammer.

00:09:05.260 --> 00:09:06.650
I should keep it a secret.

00:09:07.260 --> 00:09:11.220
If I don't, dad will be more heartbroken than I've ever seen,

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:13.060
not to mention furious.

00:09:23.860 --> 00:09:27.820
But why is my father like that?

00:09:29.610 --> 00:09:33.530
No matter whether he's happy or
 angry, it's always the same.

00:09:34.370 --> 00:09:36.040
He's rough every time.

00:09:36.660 --> 00:09:40.820
He's savage and stormy enough for a whole band of robbers!

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:20.370
But I want to be with my brother.

00:10:20.960 --> 00:10:24.460
Even if I have to do it in secret.

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:32.340
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:10:28.340 --> 00:10:32.340
Ronja, the Robber's Daughter

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:39.850
Ronja!

00:10:42.330 --> 00:10:43.780
I'm so happy.

00:10:44.360 --> 00:10:46.900
You really did get better.

00:10:46.900 --> 00:10:48.850
I'm truly surprised and overjoyed!

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:55.370
What's wrong? Are you still feeling ill?

00:10:56.530 --> 00:10:58.450
Not at all.

00:10:58.450 --> 00:11:00.080
I'm all better.

00:11:01.750 --> 00:11:03.250
I see.

00:11:18.260 --> 00:11:20.720
I can't sneak back into the forest when it's like this.

00:11:29.860 --> 00:11:32.860
But I've had enough of that place for a while.

00:11:35.820 --> 00:11:39.370
I didn't know that not being able to meet would be so painful.

00:11:40.370 --> 00:11:43.770
It's like we're living a thousand kilometers apart.

00:11:47.130 --> 00:11:50.420
This snow is such a pain!

00:12:09.820 --> 00:12:14.070
Sturkus and I went to draw water yesterday.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:18.780
So it has to be someone else who goes this time!

00:12:19.490 --> 00:12:20.580
Ouch!

00:12:23.300 --> 00:12:24.960
What are you saying?!

00:12:24.960 --> 00:12:29.080
Using a lottery to pick shifts was your idea in the first place!

00:12:34.420 --> 00:12:37.840
So we'll decide by lottery this morning as well!

00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:42.850
But no matter what you say, two days in a row is just awful!

00:12:43.850 --> 00:12:47.690
Klippen! Have you no kindness?

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.200
Show some sympathy!

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:52.320
I'm also opposed to the lottery.

00:12:53.030 --> 00:12:57.040
Did anyone else here have to draw water more than ten times this winter?

00:12:57.660 --> 00:12:58.740
See?

00:13:00.320 --> 00:13:01.910
Nobody did.

00:13:01.910 --> 00:13:05.370
If I have to go one more time, I'll die.

00:13:05.370 --> 00:13:07.000
Who cares?!

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.880
Ten times or a hundred times, it doesn't matter. A lottery is a lottery!

00:13:12.920 --> 00:13:16.340
Since it's come down to this, we should settle it with our fists!

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:18.200
Fine, let's do it.

00:13:18.880 --> 00:13:21.390
Bring it on!

00:13:26.100 --> 00:13:29.890
I know breakfast is over, but you're fighting already?!

00:13:33.610 --> 00:13:37.030
You're as idle as oxen!

00:13:37.030 --> 00:13:41.700
You should be working hard, even when you're not on the job!

00:13:43.080 --> 00:13:44.950
Fjosok! Sturkus!

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:48.040
If you don't want to draw water—
fine—then clean the roof.

00:13:48.540 --> 00:13:53.040
Every roof on the castle, make sure you do them all!

00:13:53.840 --> 00:13:57.590
Klippen and Tjorm, you bring straw to the horse stables.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:02.090
Knotas, you carry firewood to the kitchen.

00:14:02.090 --> 00:14:04.890
Pelje, go and tend to the baby goats.

00:14:04.890 --> 00:14:07.680
Remember, there's one that doesn't drink milk.

00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:30.540
We're never doing a lottery again!

00:14:42.380 --> 00:14:44.930
Hey, it's your turn.

00:14:56.900 --> 00:14:59.530
I lost again, huh?

00:14:59.530 --> 00:15:03.200
You might just have a talent for gambling.

00:15:07.740 --> 00:15:12.460
Alright, shall we play "Murktroll's Nose" next?

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:25.720
Ah, before that, I need to quickly relieve myself.

00:15:26.180 --> 00:15:29.350
It's a bother that us old people have to go so frequently.

00:15:44.570 --> 00:15:47.870
I can't play dice forever.

00:16:25.570 --> 00:16:27.660
There's no way I can jump this now...

00:17:18.710 --> 00:17:20.790
Skalle-Per once told me...

00:17:21.380 --> 00:17:27.510
this is where the master of this castle kept prisoners a long time ago.

00:17:30.050 --> 00:17:32.010
They could never again see the light of day,

00:17:32.470 --> 00:17:35.470
and were left here until they died.

00:18:05.210 --> 00:18:08.630
This part here is right under Hell's Gap.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:11.050
That night of thunder when you were born

00:18:11.050 --> 00:18:18.140
split the castle in two, and all of the rubble fell here.

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:22.440
So this underground passage is now a dead end.

00:18:22.440 --> 00:18:25.740
Listen, Ronja. Here you must...

00:18:26.650 --> 00:18:29.030
Here you must stop.

00:18:36.700 --> 00:18:41.500
But on the other side, the passage continues on.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:46.210
I want to go to the other side.

00:18:48.210 --> 00:18:54.090
Birk might be somewhere beyond all this rubble!

00:19:06.610 --> 00:19:09.990
I haven't seen Ronja that much lately.

00:19:09.990 --> 00:19:13.450
What is she up to, and where does she go?

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:17.280
She's reckless, so she goes everywhere.

00:19:17.990 --> 00:19:20.790
I think she's shoveling snow or something.

00:20:18.760 --> 00:20:22.470
If I meet Birk again I can talk to him.

00:20:24.140 --> 00:20:29.650
Also, I could find out whether or not...

00:20:30.820 --> 00:20:39.280
he really does want to be my brother, like we promised in the snowstorm that day.

00:21:04.810 --> 00:21:06.730
After today...

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:11.480
I'm never carrying stones again,

00:21:11.480 --> 00:21:18.200
no matter how big or small.

00:21:56.780 --> 00:22:00.710
Why?! I hate these stones so much!

00:22:00.710 --> 00:22:04.530
They should just melt away!

00:22:17.340 --> 00:22:22.970
Thus, Ronja carried stones day after day.

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:25.310
And then...

00:22:53.830 --> 00:22:59.710
Ronja could feel that she was heading down a dangerous path.

00:23:00.880 --> 00:23:06.640
But there was nothing so dangerous that she would not try it in order to reach Birk.

00:23:08.070 --> 00:23:12.850
Ronja longed for him.

